WEBVTT

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.380
Hear me, humans!

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.880
I shall leave Ente Isla in your hands today!

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.960
But know this: I shall return

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.550
to subjugate you and all of Ente Isla!

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.110
So, they've fled through the Gate.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.730
What shall we do?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:28.980
Follow them, obviously.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:34.910
You do realize we have no idea what's on the other side?

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.540
I don't care what world he runs to--it won't do any good.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.370
I <i>will</i> find him.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.010
I'll find him, and I'll defeat him with my own hands.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.600
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:12.650
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.700
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:33.300
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.760
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:44.930
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:50.730
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.400
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.780
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.320
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:05.620
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:13.550
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:30.020
Why are you working part-time at the Hatagaya MgRonald's, Satan?

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.400
Emilia the hero? Forget me, what are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:39.280
I leapt through the Gate after you, in order to take you down.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.870
Emilia, wait, I can explain!

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.370
I don't want to hear it. Prepare to die, Satan!

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.040
Hey, Emilia.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.710
Shut up. I'm not going to chat with you!

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.510
It's just, that knife...

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.930
Isn't that from the 100-yen shop in Sasazuka?

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.220
S-So what?!

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.060
What happened to your sacred sword?

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.690
Th-That's none of your business!

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.860
Have you lost your celestial force, by any chance?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.860
Or maybe you just can't afford to waste it?

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.980
Well, you're in the same boat, aren't you?!

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:20.990
The magic I sense from you now is nothing compared to what it was in Ente Isla!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.780
Well, yeah...

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.450
Sword or no sword, a Devil with no magic

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.830
who's working fast-food jobs is hardly a formidable adversary!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.040
Prepare yourself!

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.090
Oh dear. Those are precious ingredients...

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.970
His Majesty sure is late.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.930
"Metropolitan Police Department

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.930
East Yoyogi Police Station"

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.930
"West Sasazuka Outpost"

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.850
Well? Why were you fighting in the middle of the street?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.890
To take him down.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.640
"Take him down"?

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.940
Look, I don't know what your boyfriend did,

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.360
but whatever it was, no knife fights!

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.650
B-Boyfriend?

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.450
He probably thinks that was a lovers' quarrel or something.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.160
I am <i>not</i> in a romantic relationship with this man!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.540
Fine, but if you're breaking up,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.710
you need to just talk it over like reasonable adults, okay?

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.800
I'll let you slide for today.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:20.760
Huh?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:25.180
But just this once. I've memorized your address.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:29.180
Tonight will be the last good night's sleep you'll ever have.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.600
Hey, that doesn't sound like the kind of thing a hero should say.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.360
I don't want to hear that from a part-timer Devil!

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.360
Whatever, give me back my umbrella, you 100-yen hero!

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.280
You said I could toss it when I was done.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.530
I took it neatly apart and put it in the trash for you.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.280
How could you?!

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.660
I'm a hero; I wouldn't leave an umbrella from the Devil just lying around.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.620
Wh-What a pain...

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.880
Anyway, starting tomorrow you'd better watch your back at night!

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.090
She sure doesn't seem heroic to me...

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.850
Yes, Sir, in that case--

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.060
I'm sorry, Ma'am.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.430
Please select "Call Rate" from the menu--

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:18.270
Again, my name is Yusa, and I thank you for allowing me to assist you today.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.650
Aw, man, there are way too many complaints today!

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.360
Try cracking open the manual for a change, why don't you!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:28.870
Hey, wanna grab lunch at that new curry place that opened last week?

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.160
Hmm, it might be crowded this time of day...

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:35.290
Okay then, should we give up and do MgR's for today?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.130
Anything but that. Sorry.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.800
"Answer"

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:39.340
Ugh, another one.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.750
Oh, well. Back to work!

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:46.590
Thank you for calling the Docodemo Customer
Service Center. How may I help you?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.540
It's time for "Crash That Dinner!"

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:22.960
All right, let's visit this house here!

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:27.720
Wow, suddenly I'm smelling something lovely!

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:31.600
Why, this is just sumptuous!
Is that steak I see?! Lovely!

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.810
Are you celebrating something today?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.770
Now I see why it smells so good!
Look here, cameraman!

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.600
You're using high-quality meat, aren't you, Ma'am?

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.320
Could this be a cut that costs 20,000 yen a gram?

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.940
No? It's not?!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:50.110
--Argh, at this rate I'm doing the same thing <i>he</i> is!
--Ninety-eight yen?! You're kidding!

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.040
Wish we had a little more protein.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:00.250
You eat hamburgers on almost a daily basis, Sire.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.040
The MHK guy?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.590
He came yesterday.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:05.760
Newspaper salesman?

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:12.140
I would think they're fully aware that we can't afford a subscription...

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.520
Hello, to whom do we owe the pleasure?

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:23.980
Well, I thank you for that most courteous greeting, Demon General Alciel.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:27.650
You <i>do</i> remember Emilia the hero, I assume?

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.200
E-Emilia the hero?!

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.080
Now open this door right now!
Accept your punishment with good grace!

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:35.990
Hey!

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.210
--Sire! It's the hero! The hero is here!
--How dare you lock me out!

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:41.920
--Y-Yeah, I know.
--Come on, open up!

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:44.920
--Did you <i>know</i> about this, Sire?
--You're in there too, aren't you, Satan?!
Give up and open this door!

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.050
--Yeah. Sorry I didn't tell you.
--Hey! Hurry up!

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.760
--I ran into her yesterday on my way home from work.
--I'll kick this thing open! You okay with that?

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.470
I'll kick it!

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.970
--The police mistook it for a lovers' quarrel.
--You want that?!

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:02.150
I've never been so mortified in my life!
Me, dating the ruler of demons?!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:05.940
--Open up! Let me in right now!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.360
--And might I ask why you didn't tell me, Sire?

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.360
--I'm getting it out!

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.440
--Well, I figured she didn't do any real damage, so...
--I'm getting <i>it</i> out, you hear me?!

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:14.530
--And it looked like she couldn't use her powers, just like we can't.
--Open up! Hey! Hurry up...

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.030
--Open the door!

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:19.950
--The hero has no way to replenish her heavenly power in this world, either...

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.950
--Hey! Come on...

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.790
--In other words, she has no power to control the gate?
--Hey...!

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.130
Aw, let her in.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.590
I swear I'll kick it in...

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.800
This room is awful...

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.470
It's shabby, it's tiny, and it's got paper-thin walls.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.970
Wow, that's just mean.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.270
The Devil's Castle prioritizes functionality over comfort.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.190
"Functionality"? That's a laugh.
And what's with the pathetic dinner?

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:52.150
Hey, Ashiya is amazing! He whips up meals out of nothing, almost like magic!

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.360
I am honored by your kind praise, Sire.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.120
No prob.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.450
Are you stupid?

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.240
I can't believe the ruler of demons is dining on konjac and cucumbers!

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.790
Got a problem with that? We're poor.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:03.830
<i>Yes</i>, I do!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.210
Did I seriously travel to another world to kill a broken-down guy like this?!

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:12.130
It's pathetic! Even I live better than <i>this</i>, and I live alone!

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:13.420
Your comrades aren't here?

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.010
Shut up!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:20.680
One of the high priests was supposed to come with me.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:24.810
We were going to come home as soon as we defeated you!

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.230
But then... But then...!

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.070
Olba, hurry! The gate's about to close!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.820
I can see that!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.490
Make it in time...

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.790
We made it, Olba!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.200
Olba?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.830
No way!

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.330
Olba!

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.790
I ended up coming here alone.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.050
That's rough.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.670
I don't want your <i>pity.</i>

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.550
You're like a search party that needs its own search party.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.810
Well, I guess you'd better find a way home fast.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.180
You may have found us, but we don't have the money to move anywhere else.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:06.230
That's why we're living here.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:10.610
I'm beginning my new attempt at world conquest from this Devil's Castle!

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:13.320
Can you? You don't even have a full-time job.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:18.490
If you think I'm just living a peaceful part-timer's life, you're dead wrong.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.530
I intend to conquer Japan!

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.500
For your information,

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.830
MgRonald's has a system where part-timers can become regular employees!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.630
Hear me, Emilia: I shall become a regular employee in this world!

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.220
And thus I shall accumulate wealth and social status,

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:39.180
become a powerful figure who makes all manner of humans kneel before me,

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:42.050
and then invade Ente Isla once more!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.560
That's ludicrous.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:51.520
I'm sure a mere human like you can't understand my lofty aims.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:55.480
I suspect she understands all too well, Sire.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.150
Somehow I just don't care anymore.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.700
I'm going home. I have work tomorrow.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.580
Don't go getting the wrong idea, though.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:07.000
If I used my remaining power,
I could kill you any time I wanted.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.960
So why don't you?

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.920
Because if I use it all up, I won't be able to get home to Ente Isla.

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.960
So I'll let you live until
I figure out my way home.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:22.550
Oh, and in Japan my name is Emi Yusa. Don't slip up.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:29.520
What's with the name "Sadao," anyway?

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.560
Nobody in this generation is named that!

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.400
Apologize to all the Sadaos in Japan for that!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.500
Emi, you've been really stressed lately, haven't you?

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.630
Wanna go get a bite to eat after work?

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.920
Hmmm... Well, I have something to do this evening...

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.470
So, did you finally get a boyfriend?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.550
It's not like that!

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:13.020
There's no way the Devil is just innocently living the poor life.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.060
I can't let him out of my sight.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.030
Aw, come on, you can just go by yourself!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:23.110
I cannot do this alone!
The task requires your powers, Sire.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.160
Come, let us hurry!

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.040
Jeez, it's fine, they're not gonna run out!

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.540
You don't take this battle seriously enough!

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.790
Where are they going at this time of day?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:41.300
Let's get back in line later and buy one more carton each.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:43.550
No, that's against the rules.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.930
Emi, want to go out to dinner tonight?

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:53.770
Sorry, I have to run some errands.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.770
Ashiya, I'm leaving you behind!

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.940
There's no time to waste!
We're going to the bath!

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:05.660
--Please, Sire, wait! I just need to lock the door!
--As in <i>blood</i> bath? Who are they fighting?!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.580
Phew, we made it in time.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:14.540
Man, I wish they'd keep bathhouses open 24 hours!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:19.630
Maybe when I conquer Japan, my first act will be to make a 24-hour one!

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.430
Come on, you'll come out with me <i>tonight</i>, right?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.090
Hmm? U-Umm...

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:28.390
You're busy again?!

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.470
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.730
So, you put men before friendship.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.890
I told you, it's not like that!

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.690
Sire, please don't!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.770
But anyone would be curious about this demonic experiment!

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:44.280
"Demonic," my foot! Quit being ridicu--

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.200
Whoa, it's just like Chi said!

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.870
You try some, too! It <i>does</i> taste like melon! Just a little!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.460
"Melon," my foot!

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:59.880
--A cucumber is a cucumber, whether you put honey on it or not!
--Maybe I'll go home...

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.750
Now you listen to me, Sire!

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.010
Only people with leeway in their budgets can eat like this!

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.510
Don't you have any leeway in your heart?

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.800
I don't appreciate the snarky comeback!

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.970
In any case, if you crave melon enough to mix cucumbers and honey,

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:17.190
you're better off just buying a melon!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:18.600
What is it?

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:19.980
An earthquake.

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.610
Don't try to distract me!

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:24.990
Sheesh, what's your problem?

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.070
Don't you "sheesh" me! Sheesh!

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.240
--Teehee!
--King Satan!

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.370
Welcome.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:38.540
May I have a moment?

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.920
Are you ready to order, Miss?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.550
I need to speak with you outside.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.300
Takeout, got it.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:47.720
When you get off work, meet me at the intersection where we met.

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.390
I won't take no for an answer.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.180
Would you like to make that a meal?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.350
Come alone.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.890
Okay, just the sandwich, then.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.810
One Big Mag burger, please!

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.560
I don't plan to fight you. Make sure you show up.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:04.440
Thanks a bunch! Step over to the side, please, it'll be right out!

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:11.570
What a pain.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.450
That customer was kind of weird, huh?

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.330
Yep. It takes all kinds, as they say.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:21.420
It looked like you two were talking about something. Do you know her?

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.380
We have a bit of a history.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.840
I'm suspicious!

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:26.760
Why?

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:31.340
She was sort of pretty, wasn't she?
Wasn't she?! <i>Wasn't</i> she, Mr. Maou?!

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.680
Don't say "wasn't she" three times!

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.720
What's with you, Chi? She and I aren't--

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.310
Welcome to MgRonald's! I can take your order whenever you're ready.

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.820
I'm heading out, Mr. Maou!

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:48.320
Mmm! Night, Chi!

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.320
Good niiiight!

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:51.360
Mr. Maou!

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:52.450
Yeah?

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.740
Were you okay in yesterday's earthquake?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:55.950
Earthquake?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.790
Oh, yeah, there was one.
My roommate didn't feel it, though.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.580
Roommate?!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:04.710
--What do you mean, "okay"?
--What? Are we talking about the roommate?

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.090
No, the earthquake.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:09.590
What? Oh! It hit my place really hard.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:14.050
When I got home from school, all my books and CDs had fallen off the shelves.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:17.430
Huh?! The earthquake wasn't that big!

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.680
Yes, I asked my friends at school, too,

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.850
but for some reason it was only my place that got hit hard.

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.190
By the way, Mr. Maou!

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.400
Wha-- Yes?!

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:29.860
A minute ago--you said something about a roommate--!

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:30.940
Y-Yeah...

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:37.490
Might that roommate be of a g-g-g-girlfriendly sort?!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:43.080
Nah, a guy. I'm living the poor life with an old servant--I mean, <i>friend</i> of mine.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.880
Oh, I see! Thank goodness!

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:48.170
For what?!

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:58.760
Well? What do you want to talk about?

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:01.600
I want you to tell me something:

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:05.310
Would you like to live in this world forever?

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.560
Excuse me?!

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:10.320
Of course not! Where did <i>that</i> come from?

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:15.360
I've seen your attitude at work and at home over the past several days.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.660
Are you a stalker now?

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.160
You haven't done anything evil, and you're living a simple, serious life.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:23.830
You're trusted by your manager and younger coworkers alike,

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.670
and you deal with customers with an ease supported by confidence.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:30.460
You're the ideal MgR's worker.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.460
Am I from Kansai now?

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:37.430
I was ready to write off what you said the other day as a joke,

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.350
but now I'm starting to think there was some truth to it.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:45.850
If you're willing to spend the rest of your life in this world,

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:49.440
I don't feel a need to defeat you just for the sake of it.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.360
Why don't you stay in Sasazuka for good?

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:58.070
Is telling men to live with other men forever a thing for you or something?

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:03.870
Give up on Ente Isla and find a new life here.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.370
Not a chance.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:08.920
I swear I'll return to conquer Ente Isla.

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:21.470
--Pathetic... Is he really the Devil?

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:18.390
--Wh-What?

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.470
--Gah, a flat tire?! Get it together, Dullahan!

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:24.980
You died right after I bought you!

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.610
What's with the melodrama?
You can get a flat fixed for 1,000 yen!

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:32.980
Really?! Then I'll go first thing in the morning and--

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.150
Hey, are we...

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.740
...being shot at?!

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:43.120
There are holes in the sign!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.870
Hey, don't touch me!

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:47.210
Is this really the time to argue?!

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.380
Heh, you're pretty good.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:53.170
I <i>am</i> a hero, you know. Don't underestimate me.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.960
So, would you mind getting off of me?

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.720
You're the one who let me land on you!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:04.140
There should still be plenty of people at Sasazuka Station. Can you run?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.180
I'm faster than you are, guy who takes it easy riding a bike.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.270
You're on. Let's go!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:20.660
Guess they're... not following us this far, huh...?

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.620
What was that about?

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:26.950
Dunno, but... that was no ordinary sniper...

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.870
Those bullets were made of magic energy.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.540
Magic?! Which means...

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.420
We're dealing with someone pretty powerful.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.220
And someone who knows who we are.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.510
Is there such a person?

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:44.300
A mystery sniper just showed up when a demon king and a hero were in one place.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:47.770
The natural assumption is that this has to do with Ente Isla.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.850
Look at the trouble you got me into!

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.190
Y-You think it's my fault?!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:57.190
If you'd picked a safer place and time, this wouldn't have happened.

00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:00.490
That's <i>your</i> fault for working so late!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.030
Why not meet in the afternoon?

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.530
I work in the afternoon!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.910
Well don't blame me for that!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:10.160
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.290
Home. Gotta be at work early tomorrow.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.040
You're just going to run off by yourself?!

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:16.840
Of course!

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:20.090
You be careful getting home, too. See you!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:28.310
Look, do you intend to launch a night raid or something?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.430
N-No.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:35.110
Then what's the big idea?
Our landlady lives right next door!

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.690
I'd rather avoid her, so no making a scene, okay?

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:43.280
Wh-What is it?

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:46.870
I-It makes my blood boil to ask you this...

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.250
And more importantly it's a breach of faith with the <i>world</i>, but...

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:53.500
Did you come here just to provoke me?!

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:57.000
Would you le... le...

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.550
"Le"?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:08.350
Le... let me stay the night here?

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:11.850
I... dropped my wallet...

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.690
Emilia the hero?!

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:20.030
It's okay; she doesn't have the energy to fight right now.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.570
How can you be so complacent, Sire?!

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:25.490
You are a ruler of demons! You cannot party the night away with some <i>hero</i>!

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:30.120
We just got attacked.
Someone shot at us with magic bullets.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:31.290
Magic?!

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:35.290
So, she says she dropped her wallet while we were running away.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:39.750
Apparently she lives over by Eifukucho.
That's a long walk, you know?

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.970
Are you saying she's staying here for the night, Sire?!

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.220
Don't just stand there, come in.

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:48.010
Th-Thank you for having me.

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:53.730
Just sit wherever. FYI, don't expect any luxuries like a guest futon.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.600
I know, jeez.

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:59.650
What kind of attitude is that?!
King Satan is treating you with benevolence!

00:21:59.860 --> 00:22:02.610
Pipe down, Ashiya, or the landlady will show up.

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:05.200
Emi, take this.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:11.660
That's the same detergent I use...

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:14.710
If you want a pillow, use some magazines.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:19.670
I'll lend you 1,000 yen for now, so get out of here on the first bus.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:21.170
Okay.

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:25.090
The king graciously lent you those thousand yen out of his meager savings!

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:26.430
Treat it with respect!

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:31.510
Yeah, yeah! I'll leave in the morning, okay?! Thanks for the loan!

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:33.520
Wench...

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:36.020
--We should turn in, too.
--Yes, Sire.

00:22:36.230 --> 00:22:40.690
I haven't let my guard down!
Don't try any funny business!

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:44.820
Why am I doing this?

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:01.920
We were pretty miserable at first, too, you know?

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:03.380
Yes, Sire.

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:09.260
And we were okay because there were two of us, but it sounds like she's alone...

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:12.300
You've grown soft, King Satan.

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:19.060
Who's this from?

00:23:19.270 --> 00:23:20.480
Earthquakes?

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:22.770
What is this?

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:25.570
Oh, I've got one from Chi too.

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:29.780
"There's going to be another earthquake. What do I do?" Huh?

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:31.410
Sire?

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.540
What's going on?

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:58.560
<i>Where will morning start from, in this quiet sky?</i>

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:04.190
<i>Fingertips twining in a pinky</i> <i>swear I pretended not to see</i>

00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:14.400
<i>If the moon's been laughed at,</i> <i>she'll sink away toward yesterday</i>

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:20.330
<i>Liar, coward--if I'm all these things at once</i>

00:24:20.540 --> 00:24:26.040
<i>Then I only blossomed in dreams</i>

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:31.590
<i>I hid in the moon's shadow,</i> <i>but the truth is, I was crying</i>

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:37.310
<i>The tears won't flow anymore--</i> <i>did they all dry up?</i>

00:24:37.510 --> 00:24:43.850
<i>If I could forgive everything,</i> <i>maybe they'd flow again</i>

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:51.400
<i>But these are all things I want to protect</i>
